\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 378929, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01N6nhKPH1LpJHteSo5oUm5x", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 378929, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01N6nhKPH1LpJHteSo5oUm5x", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383184, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened pull request #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` said in its description that it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66, which made `tests/test_money.py` fail.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't find FIN-212 in the security advisory lookup, which may just mean it's tracked somewhere else. I relied on the requirement as stated in the test and the code's description.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01E4mXztB76jTHCdG9yhHm3E", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018YpyPjiE5cXu4AgdLorCYm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence":