ND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring said otherwise.\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Now e.g. 2.665 rounds to 2.66 (not 2.67), and 2.675 still rounds to 2.68.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened pull request #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` said in its description that it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66, which made `tests/test_money.py` fail.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't find FIN-212 in the security advisory lookup, which may just mean it's tracked somewhere else. I relied on the requirement as stated in the test and the code's description.", "type": "text"}]}]}